# [Life Is A Drag]

A short 3D dialogue-driven prototype built in Unity focused dialogue system, interaction triggers, and scene transitions.

## What's in it

- Dialogue system using Yarn Spinner
- Per-character text blip audio
- Scene transitions with fading black screen
- Player movement locked during dialogue

## Screenshots / GIF

[One image or GIF of the game. Even a static screenshot helps.]

## How to run

1. Clone the repo
2. Open in Unity 6000.3.8f1
3. Open `Assets/Scenes/Main Menu.unity`
4. Press Play

## Controls

- A and D — Move Left/Right
- F — Interact
- Space - Continue dialogue
- Up/Down Arrow Keys - Navigate dialogue choices
- Enter - Select a choice


## What I'd improve with more time

- Animations for player and NPCs during dialogue
- More variety of animations for idling NPCs
- Cleaner 'BlipType' lookup
- Better dialogue UI
- Loading screen between scene transitions
- Integrate QTE mechanics to gameplay and UI (base class already exists)
- Expand more on story content

